{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelConfluence","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Sqrt","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.balanced_kernel_tendsto_schwinger_of_confluence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.balanced_kernel_tendsto_schwinger_of_confluence","kind":"theorem","line":304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedMomentConfluence.lean#L304-L328","doc":"**Balanced-kernel weak convergence with `hmom` DISCHARGED** — the\ncorollary of the merged `balanced_kernel_tendsto_schwinger` in which the\nbare moment-convergence hypothesis `hmom` is *replaced by the proved\nper-`n` confluence*: if the kernels' Stieltjes moments are the balanced\nnormalizers at fibre parameters `qs j → 1` (hypothesis `hrep` — the\nconjecture's open (REP) representability content), then the kernels\nconverge weakly to the unit Schwinger measure `e^{−s}·ds`, conditional\nonly on the two classical Mathlib-gap classes. The hypothesis surface\nshrinks: moment *convergence* is now a theorem\n(`tendsto_balancedNormalizerR_seq`); what remains is *representability*\n(`hrep`) plus the two named classical theorems. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.BalancedH2Expansion.expansion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.BalancedH2Expansion.expansion","kind":"theorem","line":296,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedMomentConfluence.lean#L296-L296","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.BalancedH2Expansion.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.BalancedH2Expansion.mk","kind":"ctor","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedMomentConfluence.lean#L295-L295","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.BalancedH2Expansion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.BalancedH2Expansion","kind":"class","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedMomentConfluence.lean#L284-L300","doc":"**The quantitative `h²` asymptotic (probe-exact, Lean-open) —\ncontent-bearing hypothesis class, NO instance in this repo.** The probe\nproves (sympy, exact rationals, every order tested through `h³`):\n`log(N^bal_{e^h}(n)/(n−1)!) = c₂(n)·h² + O(h⁴)` with `h¹ = h³ = 0` and\n`c₂(n) = (n−1)(n−2)(2n+3)/144` (the sum identity `sum_c2_closed_form`).\nFormalizing the remainder bound needs `Real.log`/series-expansion\nmachinery out of scope this tranche; the class carries the statement so\nany future consumer wears it in its type (§3b-cond). Fabricating an\ninstance would violate §Axiomatization-is-NOT-a-Proof. Nothing in this\nfile consumes it — the `hmom` discharge needs only the PROVED qualitative\nlimit `tendsto_balancedNormalizerR`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.sum_c2_closed_form_of_one_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.sum_c2_closed_form_of_one_le","kind":"theorem","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedMomentConfluence.lean#L274-L282","doc":"`n`-indexed form of `sum_c2_closed_form` for `n ≥ 1`:\n`c₂(n) = Σ_{k=1}^{n−1}(k²−1)/24 = (n−1)(n−2)(2n+3)/144`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.sum_c2_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.sum_c2_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedMomentConfluence.lean#L257-L272","doc":"**The `c₂(n)` closed-form sum identity** (probe C2's symbolic\nsummation, Lean-proved): with `m = n − 1`,\n`Σ_{k=1}^{m} (k²−1)/24 = m(m−1)(2m+5)/144`, i.e.\n`Σ_{k=1}^{n−1}(k²−1)/24 = (n−1)(n−2)(2n+3)/144` — Attack E's predicted\n`h²` coefficient of `log(N^bal_{e^h}(n)/(n−1)!)`. Pure finite-sum algebra\nover `ℚ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.tendsto_balancedNormalizerR_seq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.tendsto_balancedNormalizerR_seq","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedMomentConfluence.lean#L246-L253","doc":"Sequence form of the confluence: along any `qs → 1`,\n`N^bal_{qs j}(n) → (n−1)!`. This is exactly the shape of the `hmom`\nhypothesis of `balanced_kernel_tendsto_schwinger`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.tendsto_balancedNormalizerR","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.tendsto_balancedNormalizerR","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedMomentConfluence.lean#L230-L244","doc":"**The per-`n` balanced moment confluence** (the audit-§2 qualitative\nstatement, PROVED): `N^bal_q(n) → (n−1)!` as `q → 1`. The normalizer is a\nfinite product of terms continuous at `q = 1` (each `[k]_q → k`), so the\nlimit is the evaluation `[n−1]_1! = (n−1)!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.continuousAt_balancedNormalizer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.continuousAt_balancedNormalizer","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedMomentConfluence.lean#L224-L228","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.continuous_qfact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.continuous_qfact","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedMomentConfluence.lean#L215-L222","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.continuous_qint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.continuous_qint","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedMomentConfluence.lean#L211-L213","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.balancedNormalizerR","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.balancedNormalizerR","kind":"def","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedMomentConfluence.lean#L204-L209","doc":"The real balanced normalizer in the substrate variable `q`:\n`N^bal_q(n) = balancedNormalizer (√q) n`. For `q > 0` this is exactly\n`q^{−(n−1)(n−2)/4}·[n−1]_q!` (the probe's normalizer), the quarter-powers\nof `q` being integer powers of `√q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.balancedNormalizer_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.balancedNormalizer_one","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedMomentConfluence.lean#L193-L197","doc":"At `v = 1` (the confluence point `q = 1`) the balanced normalizer is\nthe classical `(n−1)!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.qfact_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.qfact_one","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedMomentConfluence.lean#L184-L191","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.qint_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.qint_one","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedMomentConfluence.lean#L181-L182","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.balancedNormalizer_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.balancedNormalizer_succ","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedMomentConfluence.lean#L166-L179","doc":"**The exact positive-kernel split** (probe C4d / audit (i)):\n`N^bal(k+1) = [k]_{q⁻¹}! · q^{k(k−1)/4}` with the half-weight factor\n`q^{k(k−1)/4}` realized as the integer power `v^{C(k,2)}`\n(`C(k,2) = k(k−1)/2`). This is the `A(k)·B(k)` factorization whose two\nfactors the probe realizes as manifestly positive kernels (Jackson\nq-Gamma × theta/log-normal). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.sq_balancedNormalizer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.sq_balancedNormalizer","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedMomentConfluence.lean#L153-L164","doc":"**Geometric-mean (squared) factorization** (probe C1b):\n`N^bal(n)² = [n−1]_{q}! · [n−1]_{q⁻¹}!` at `q = v²` — the balanced\nnormalizer is the geometric mean of the bar pair. The squared form is\nfully polynomial in `q` and needs no quarter-powers at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.balancedNormalizer_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.balancedNormalizer_inv","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedMomentConfluence.lean#L140-L151","doc":"**Bar-invariance of the balanced normalizer** (the Attack-E repair,\npreviously probe-only, now Lean-exact): the balanced form equals its\nbar-transform, `N^bal_{v⁻¹}(n) = N^bal_v(n)`. At `q = v²` this is\nbar-covariance `q ↦ q⁻¹` of the balanced q-Borel weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.balancedNormalizer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.balancedNormalizer","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedMomentConfluence.lean#L133-L138","doc":"**The balanced q-Borel normalizer in the half-variable** `v = q^{1/2}`:\n`N^bal(n) = v^{−C(n−1,2)} · [n−1]_{v²}!`. For `v² = q` this is exactly the\nprobe's `q^{−(n−1)(n−2)/4}·[n−1]_q!` — the quarter-power of `q` is the\ninteger power `C(n−1,2) = (n−1)(n−2)/2` of `v`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.pow_choose_mul_qfact_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.pow_choose_mul_qfact_inv","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedMomentConfluence.lean#L113-L131","doc":"**Bar transform of the q-factorial.**\n`q^{C(m,2)} · [m]_{q⁻¹}! = [m]_q!` (`C(m,2) = m(m−1)/2 = Nat.choose m 2`):\nthe probe's exact identity `N_q(n) = q^{(n−1)(n−2)/2}·N_{q⁻¹}(n)` in\nmultiplied (division-free) form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.pow_mul_qint_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedMomentConfluence.pow_mul_qint_inv","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedMomentConfluence.lean#L102-L111","doc":"**Bar transform of the quantum integer.**\n`q^k · [k+1]_{q⁻¹} = [k+1]_q` — the reflection `i ↦ k − i` of the\ngeometric sum, exact over any field with `q ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}